<section id="adminGuideContent" class="role-guide d-none" data-role-guide="admin" data-guide-description="Projects, deletion approvals and office settings." hidden aria-label="Admin instructions">
<p class="role-guide-context">Accounts and Staff permissions are managed by Superadmin.</p>
<h2 class="role-guide-heading" tabindex="-1">Where to click</h2>
<table class="role-guide-map" aria-label="Admin button locations"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Task</th><th scope="col">Find the control here</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Find a project</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control">View All Projects</strong> → search box</div><small class="guide-location">Left sidebar. Select a project title to open its details.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Add or edit</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>Add Project</strong> — top right of View All Projects.<span class="guide-path-line">Project title → <strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m16 3 5 5M4 20l4-1L21 6a2 2 0 0 0-5-3L3 16l-1 5Z"/></svg>Edit</strong> — bottom left of Project Details.</span></div></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Delete or review requests</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6h18M9 6V3h6v3M5 6l1 15h12l1-15M10 10v7M14 10v7"/></svg>Red trash icon</strong> on a project row.<span class="guide-path-line">Staff requests: left sidebar → <strong class="guide-control">Deletion requests</strong>.</span></div><small class="guide-location">Review first, then Continue to final confirmation.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Import or export</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control">Import</strong> / <strong class="guide-control">Export</strong> under <strong>File Options</strong></div><small class="guide-location">Above the project table, in View All Projects.</small></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Settings and backups</th><td><div class="guide-path"><strong class="guide-control">Admin</strong> in the left sidebar</div><small class="guide-location">Timeline day settings, Recent activity and Automatic project backups.</small></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p class="role-guide-profile"><strong>Your profile:</strong> top-right avatar → <strong>Edit profile</strong> or <strong>Sign out</strong>.</p><p class="role-guide-phone">On a phone, the navigation menu is at the top.</p>
<div class="role-guide-more"><h3>Extra help, if you need it</h3><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>Projects, dates, files and printing</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><p><strong>Add:</strong> enter the required project title and approved budget; add known dates and details. Choose Save Project and wait for confirmation. <strong>Edit:</strong> open a project title → Edit at bottom left → Apply Records Change. Copy important draft changes before reopening a record that another person updated.</p><p><strong>Alerts:</strong> top right of Project Details. Enter actual milestone dates in Edit after work happens. Contract durations and reminders use working days. Completion/SWA actual dates cannot be in the future. Deadline-based status updates automatically when records are loaded.</p><p><strong>Files:</strong> Edit → Attachments → add/remove → Apply Records Change. Up to 20 files per upload, 25 MB each. <strong>Print:</strong> bottom left of Project Details; printed summaries are reference copies. <strong>Logs:</strong> right side of each project row. Imports and edits are recorded in these permanent Logs; corrections add a new entry.</p><p><strong>Import:</strong> use the template, check dates and duplicates, and review results. The whole import is validated before it is saved together. A failed validation saves no projects. Undo of a completed import that created projects still requires deletion approval. <strong>Export:</strong> uses current filters across all matching pages. Archive/Restore is beside each project; archived records stay in Historical Archive.</p></div></details><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>Deletion approval and clearing history</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><p><strong>Delete directly:</strong> project-row red trash icon → review records → Continue to final confirmation → tick the checkbox → Confirm deletion. This final action removes the selected project, its history and attachments.</p><p><strong>Review Staff requests:</strong> left sidebar → Deletion requests → Review request. Check the requester, reason and records. Continue to final confirmation approves and opens the last step; Reject request keeps the records. Go back/close stops before deletion. Approved requests remain Active until finished or withdrawn.</p><p><strong>Clear request history:</strong> Deletion requests → History → Clear history clears all outcomes/pages from your own view and keeps active approvals and other users’ views. <strong>Recent activity → Clear history</strong> is different: it clears the shared visible activity list for Admin accounts while retaining older entries.</p><p>Delete all records is at the bottom of View All Projects under Data Management and also requires review and final confirmation. Archive when records need to remain retrievable.</p></div></details><details class="role-guide-detail"><summary>Admin tools, recovery and your account</summary><div class="role-guide-detail-body"><p><strong>Timeline:</strong> left sidebar → Admin → Timeline day settings → Save timeline days. Use the shared working-day calendar; changes affect reminder lead times.</p><p><strong>Backups:</strong> Admin → Automatic project backups. @if(config('tracker.cloud'))Choose Back up projects now, then Download latest backup to keep a copy. Backups use private cloud storage.@else Choose a server destination using Browse or Use default, then Back up projects now.@endif Check the result and latest backup. Automatic copies require the server scheduler.</p><p>Project backups include deletion approvals, import workflow and general activity. They exclude accounts/passwords, profile photos and settings. Ask IT for a full-system backup and restore test.</p><p>Accounts, passwords and Staff permissions are managed by Superadmin. Your top-right avatar opens Edit profile and Sign out. Admin has a 30-minute inactivity timeout and eight-hour session limit. Sign in with the same account in the same tab to review a recovered draft after a timeout.</p></div></details></div>
</section>
